{"availability":"available","full":"mylofi/qr-data-sync","name":"qr-data-sync","description":"Browser-only utils for sharing/synchronizing data using \"animated\" QR codes","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":86,"forks":4,"created":"2024-03-23T22:24:32Z","updated":"2024-08-09T15:28:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mylofi.github.io/qr-data-sync/","topics":["camera","data","qrcode","qrcode-scanner","sharing","sync","vite-plugin","webpack-plugin"],"demo":"https://mylofi.github.io/qr-data-sync/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:53.549Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:53.549Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:14:53.549Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:14.997Z","stars":86,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-10T13:01:26.667Z","stars":86,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-16T07:14:53.549Z","stars":86,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["QR-Data-Sync is a browser library with utils for sharing/synchronizing data via \"animated\" QR codes.","Any set of data that can be serialized into a string -- such as an object that's JSON-serializable -- can be broken up into a series of QR codes (of equal length, with padding for visual consistency), which can then be displayed in rapid succession, as if the code is \"animated\".","A camera on another device, with a scanning library designed to read multiple QR codes in succession, can then read these animated QR code \"frames\", and re-assemble the original data set on the other device."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mylofi/qr-data-sync/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"242a4c453894a759928d70a8482c0e26ecc06a2ea3597c612393b476644fb32d","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:15.093Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:15.093Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"QR-Data-Sync is a browser library with utils for sharing/synchronizing data via \"animated\" QR codes.","sourceUrl":"https://git